                        "entry_id": "4e6b8ca4-5f0d-36d3-942b-96163571cdc9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Approaching winter or during the approach of winter;"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "73c5cc54-683b-438b-a243-7be8afe08db6",
                                "sense_id": "147f6326-5a97-3361-86a5-578879a19072",
                                "text": "One by one the summer resident birds depart; the migrants come through in a rush, the peak of each species' wave reached nearly in a week from the first one seen; the other or winterward side of the wave declines more slowly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2a78f7a-cb20-4cb7-8c48-af0605813a59",
                                "sense_id": "147f6326-5a97-3361-86a5-578879a19072",
                                "text": "Oh, dear God, how lovely this flower, this strange youngness is the last-born wilding of the winterward grass."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "088ec5e2-2a98-4ae5-b4e2-52d9f5555ecf",
                                "sense_id": "147f6326-5a97-3361-86a5-578879a19072",
                                "text": "The latter exhibit increased sensitivity to the temperature rise, associated with increases of winter runoff owing to snow melting and decreases of summer runoff owing to both a winterward shift of spring snowmelt runoff and an enhanced […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ea5a9f72-ca8e-3a56-b9e7-3373192f6a82",
                        "entry_id": "4e6b8ca4-5f0d-36d3-942b-96163571cdc9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Becoming wintry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "763bd4c7-f754-470e-a6e7-36fa6b677f32",
                                "sense_id": "ea5a9f72-ca8e-3a56-b9e7-3373192f6a82",
                                "text": "You said the wind through the trees Named the winterward soul."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9fce17f0-23fa-4ea7-87ae-0204e5c10962",
                                "sense_id": "ea5a9f72-ca8e-3a56-b9e7-3373192f6a82",
                                "text": "It had a dying sweetness, a funereal majesty, a winterward regret."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b271769-204b-49f7-96f6-4f130547ef71",
                                "sense_id": "ea5a9f72-ca8e-3a56-b9e7-3373192f6a82",
                                "text": "O anointed with dust, What dry in your throat makes barren your tongue This winterward moment my presence has sung?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16e90814-8358-417e-8439-9ef86b7f1a2e",
                                "sense_id": "ea5a9f72-ca8e-3a56-b9e7-3373192f6a82",
                                "text": "The winterward heart moves to solstice with the stark sense that, tilted too far from its sun, it will chill."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "9f2329c0-9566-3155-97d4-2e16b5ac40e3",
